 "narrative": [
  "The major consists of ninety-six units, with forty units from lower-division courses and fifty-six units from upper-division courses.",
  "Lower division: All courses must be taken for a letter grade and passed with a minimum grade of C–.",
  "Upper division: Students must complete fifty-six upper-division units. All courses must be taken for a letter grade unless offered Pass/Not Pass only. A minimum grade of C– is required.",
  "Students may not combine business data science with a minor in business (RSM-MN-002) or data science (DSC-MN-001).",
  "Recommended: students take the capstone as near as possible to graduation.",
  "The data science and business data science majors are “selective.” Continuing students must complete the screening courses MATH 18 or MATH 31AH, MATH 20C or MATH 31BH, and DSC 10.",
  "Students majoring or minoring in any of the computer science engineering programs (CSE-BS-001/ECE-BS-001, CSE-BS-002, CSE-BS-003, CSE-BS-004, CSE MN-001) may not double major or minor in data science or business data science. Students may not double major in data science and business data science.",
  "Students will be expected to fulfill all prerequisites for all courses, which may entail additional course work beyond the data science major requirements.",
  "Also described on the Rady School of Management page (MGT-ug), which lists DSC 10/R and DSC 20/R (allowing DSC 10R, DSC 20R) where the Data Science page lists DSC 10 and DSC 20, and adds that the major cannot be paired with the computer science minor."
 ]
